; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Rainbow Random Walk
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     random, walk, color, distance, towards
; SUMMARY:  A turtle wanders at random, changing color as it goes, and turns home when it strays too far.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The turtle takes thousands of little steps, turning a random
;   amount before each one. Its pen color slowly changes through
;   the rainbow, so the scribble shows where it went first and last.
;   When it gets too far from the middle it turns back toward home.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Every walk is different.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * RANDOM to choose a turn
;   * DISTANCE and TOWARDS to steer back to a point
;   * REPCOUNT to know which step we are on
;   * a rainbow made with SIN
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Only allow turns of 90 degrees: right 90 * random 4.
;   * Make the steps longer and the walk shorter.
;   * Let two turtles walk, each with its own color.
; ============================================================

; RAINBOW sets a pen color from a number. Three waves, one for red,
; one for green, one for blue, rise and fall at different times.
to rainbow :n
  setpencolor (list 128 + 127 * sin :n 128 + 127 * sin :n + 120 128 + 127 * sin :n + 240)
end

; WANDER takes :steps random steps.
to wander :steps
  repeat :steps [
    rainbow repcount / 4
    ; A turn between 40 left and 40 right
    right (random -40 40)
    forward 6
    ; Too far away? Face home again.
    if (distance [0 0]) > 270 [setheading towards [0 0]]
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [20 20 25]
setpensize 3
wander 3000
